@* The docs layout's three columns (F164.1), on Bootstrap's grid, which every site loads (ADR 0085): the site's menu,
   above the page on a phone and beside it from a large screen; the page, in a centred container in the room that is
   left (Louis: "middle column"); and the right column, on every screen, for what stands beside the page (F164.2),
   such as the site's chat docked, with the page's sections as "On this page", the same list the floating index
   reads, from an extra-large screen, under the site's ask about the page when it gives one (F164.2). *@
@using LouisAgent.Web.Components.Site.Actions
<div class="site-docs container-fluid">
    <div class="row">
        <aside class="site-docs-menu col-12 col-lg-2">@Menu</aside>
        <div class="site-docs-page col"><div class="container-xxl px-0">@ChildContent</div></div>
        <div class="site-docs-beside col-12 col-xl-2">
            @Beside
            <aside class="site-docs-sections d-none d-xl-block" aria-label="On this page">
                @if (Ask is not null)
                {
                    <div class="mb-4"><AskButton Text="@Ask.Text" Question="@Ask.Question"/></div>
                }
                <span class="site-docs-sections-label">On this page</span>
                <SectionIndex/>
            </aside>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
